CORE
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ A &&\.\.\.: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ A \*\.\.\.: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ const A\.\.\.: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
A pack expansion whose pattern is a compound type around the pack
(`A &&...', `A *...', `const A...') in a template argument of the return
type was not expanded while deducing the function template's arguments: it
became one element and the candidate was discarded.  libc++'s std::bind
has `__bind_return<..., tuple<_Args &&...>>' as operator()'s return type.
